From 87f6e690b8d0f07186f400a346e4a4ac465f72a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rial1 <ricarnuno@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:19:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(identity): capture X-User-Id via STRIX_AUTH_HEADERS +
 serialize Caido/store access

Root cause of the m0-wrapper-vuln-5 false confirm: the fixture authenticates
via the non-standard X-User-Id header, which strix's capture layer dropped
(_AUTH_HEADER_KEYS + token/auth substring test did not match it). Every captured
identity therefore had empty headers, auth_matrix diffed identical/empty
identities, returned finding_count=0 with empty pairwise_deltas, and the agent
filed evidence_class=diff from its own reasoning rather than a harness verdict.
The funnel was empty because no real observation existed.

Fixes (all unit-verified, no-LLM):
- capture.py: STRIX_AUTH_HEADERS (comma-separated) adds extra identity-bearing
  header names so X-User-Id survives capture_from_proxy/_from_login. Proven:
  UNSET -> headers {} (repro of the bug); =X-User-Id -> {'X-User-Id':'bob'}.
- tools/identity/tools.py: _STORE_LOCK serializes per-run SQLite identity-store
  access (parallel tool dispatch collided on the write lock).
- identity/store.py: busy_timeout=5000 defense-in-depth for the store writer.
- tools/proxy/caido_api.py: _CAIDO_LOCK serializes all Caido SDK access (the
  shared aiohttp transport is not concurrency-safe; overlapping calls produced
  the "A network error occurred" that made auth_matrix run partial identity sets).
- config/models.py: optional STRIX_LLM_USER_AGENT header for endpoints that
  require one (no-op unset).
- containers/docker-entrypoint.sh: degrade gracefully when no root/passwordless
  sudo (prod agent image) instead of letting set -e kill the container + Caido.

WIP anchor for the credited both-sides M0 run (openwebui-idor-memories,
VULN_MODE=1 and =0). Not merged to 'new' pending PM (Locus-1) validation of a
funnel-backed bob->mem-1 200/403 flip.
